<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================
  cr-dotnet-0010: Web.config Transformation Elimination
  ============================================================
  CLOUD READINESS REMEDIATION: This file has been refactored to
  eliminate build-time Web.config XDT transformations in favour of
  runtime configuration injection via environment variables and
  AWS Systems Manager (SSM) Parameter Store.

  WHY: XDT transformations bake environment-specific values into
  build artefacts, preventing immutable deployments and making
  true infrastructure-as-code impossible. Cloud-native deployments
  require configuration to be injected at runtime so that a single
  build artefact can be promoted across environments without rebuild.

  HOW (Debug / Development environment):
  ─────────────────────────────────────
  All settings that were previously toggled by this transformation
  file are now controlled by the following mechanisms:

  1. ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES (highest precedence at runtime)
     Set these in your local launch profile (launchSettings.json),
     AWS Elastic Beanstalk environment properties, ECS task
     definition environment section, or AWS Systems Manager
     Parameter Store paths mapped to environment variables:

     ASPNET_ENVIRONMENT              = Development
     DB_CONNECTION_STRING            = <local or dev SQL Server connection string>
     DB_EF_CONNECTION_STRING         = <local or dev EF metadata connection string>
     REDIS_CONNECTION_STRING         = <local Redis or ElastiCache endpoint>
     MACHINE_KEY_VALIDATION_KEY      = <retrieved from AWS Secrets Manager>
     MACHINE_KEY_DECRYPTION_KEY      = <retrieved from AWS Secrets Manager>
     CLOUDFRONT_CDN_URL              = <CloudFront distribution URL or empty for local>
     CSP_POLICY_HEADER               = <Content-Security-Policy value>
     MACHINE_KEY_SECRET_NAME         = UniversityLibrarySystem/MachineKey
     DB_SECRET_NAME                  = UniversityLibrarySystem/Database/ConnectionString
     SSM_PARAMETER_PATH              = /UniversityLibrarySystem/Dev/

  2. AWS SYSTEMS MANAGER PARAMETER STORE (runtime, per-environment)
     Parameters are stored under the path prefix defined by
     SSM_PARAMETER_PATH and loaded at application startup via the
     AWS SDK (AWSSDK.SimpleSystemsManagement NuGet package).

     Example parameter paths for the Debug/Development environment:
       /UniversityLibrarySystem/Dev/DbConnectionString
       /UniversityLibrarySystem/Dev/RedisConnectionString
       /UniversityLibrarySystem/Dev/CloudFrontCdnUrl
       /UniversityLibrarySystem/Dev/CspPolicyHeader

  3. DEBUG-SPECIFIC BEHAVIOUR (replaces XDT compilation transform)
     The <compilation debug="true"> attribute in Web.config is now
     controlled by the ASPNET_ENVIRONMENT environment variable.
     When ASPNET_ENVIRONMENT=Development the application startup
     code (Global.asax / Startup.cs) enables debug compilation
     programmatically, removing the need for an XDT transform.

  MIGRATION NOTES:
  ─────────────────
  • Web.Debug.config and Web.Release.config XDT files are no longer
    applied during publish. They are retained as documentation only.
  • Remove the <DependentUpon> / <None Include="Web.Debug.config">
    entries from the .csproj if you wish to exclude them from the
    build output entirely.
  • For local development, populate a .env file or set environment
    variables in your IDE launch profile instead of relying on this
    transformation file.
  • In AWS, use Elastic Beanstalk environment properties or ECS task
    definition environment variables to supply all values listed above.
  • Sensitive values (connection strings, machine keys) MUST be stored
    in AWS Secrets Manager and retrieved at runtime — never committed
    to source control or baked into build artefacts.

  ORIGINAL XDT CONTENT (preserved for reference — no longer active):
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  The original Web.Debug.config contained no active XDT transforms;
  only commented-out examples were present. The Debug environment
  relied on the base Web.config <compilation debug="true"> setting.
  That setting is now managed via the ASPNET_ENVIRONMENT variable.
  ============================================================
-->

<!--
  This file intentionally contains no active XDT transformation directives.
  All environment-specific configuration is injected at runtime via
  environment variables and AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store as
  documented in the comments above.

  To add a new environment-specific setting:
    1. Add the environment variable name to the list above.
    2. Read it in application code via Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable()
       or ConfigurationManager.AppSettings (backed by an env-var provider).
    3. Store the value in AWS SSM Parameter Store under the appropriate path.
    4. Do NOT add XDT transform directives to this file.
-->
